# FactorySense local rules. SIDs 1000000-1999999 are reserved for local use.

# Sanity rule: proves the sensor sees the boundary. Nothing in the architecture pings the gateway,
# so an ICMP echo towards it from the plant floor means an unexpected device is probing.
alert icmp $PLANT_NET any -> any any (msg:"FACTORYSENSE ICMP echo request from plant floor"; itype:8; classtype:attempted-recon; sid:1000001; rev:1;)

# The PLC is read-only by design: the gateway only reads input registers. A Modbus write seen
# on the gateway's interfaces means the gateway is compromised and being used to tamper with the machine.
alert modbus any any -> any $MODBUS_PORTS (msg:"FACTORYSENSE Modbus write attempt on read-only PLC"; modbus: access write; classtype:attempted-admin; sid:1000002; rev:1;)

# TODO(phase 2): port scan against the gateway, unexpected protocols on the plant floor,
# plaintext (non-TLS) traffic towards the broker.
